{"units": [{"id": "τέχνη-quote7", "translation": "But craft is far weaker than necessity."}, {"id": "τέχνη-quote8", "translation": "with unerring skill"}, {"id": "τέχνη-quote9", "translation": "The arts of Calchas are not unfulfilled."}, {"id": "τέχνη-quote10", "translation": "many-worded arts"}, {"id": "τέχνη-quote11", "translation": "chosen by inspired arts"}, {"id": "τέχνη-quote12", "translation": "Zeus, having created in him a mind inspired with skill"}, {"id": "τέχνη-quote13", "translation": "the prophetic art teeming"}, {"id": "τέχνη-quote14", "translation": "in what way he will be rolled out of this art"}, {"id": "τέχνη-word1", "translation": "of fortune"}, {"id": "τέχνημα-orth1", "translation": "artifice, cunning device"}, {"id": "τέχνημα-def1", "translation": "artificially made. See τεύχημα."}, {"id": "τέχνημα-def2", "translation": "artifice, trick"}, {"id": "τέχνημα-quote1", "translation": "offering huckstering tricks"}, {"id": "τέχνημα-word1", "translation": "artificially made"}, {"id": "τέχνημα-word2", "translation": "thing made, work"}, {"id": "τέως-orth1", "translation": "for a while, until now"}, {"id": "τέως-def1", "translation": "for a while, until now"}, {"id": "τέως-quote1", "translation": "a friend before, but now an enemy"}, {"id": "τηθύς-orth1", "translation": "Tethys"}, {"id": "τηθύς-def1", "translation": "Tethys, daughter of Heaven and Earth, wife of Ocean"}, {"id": "τηθύς-quote1", "translation": "offspring of Tethys of many children"}, {"id": "τηθύς-quote2", "translation": "and the children of Tethys"}, {"id": "τήκω-orth1", "translation": "to melt"}, {"id": "τήκω-def1", "translation": "I melt (transitive)"}, {"id": "τήκω-def2", "translation": "τήκομαι I am consumed, I perish"}, {"id": "τήκω-quote1", "translation": "melts the rocky snow"}, {"id": "τήκω-quote2", "translation": "and the opinions of men, even those very august under the sky, melting away upon the earth, diminish without honor"}, {"id": "τήκω-word1", "translation": "I am melting, I am wasting away"}, {"id": "τῆλε-orth1", "translation": "far off"}, {"id": "τῆλε-def1", "translation": "far off"}, {"id": "τῆλε-quote1", "translation": "far off toward the west, at the settings of lord Helios"}, {"id": "τηλέπλανος-orth1", "translation": "wandering far, leading into distant wanderings"}, {"id": "τηλέπλανος-def1", "translation": "wandering far, leading into distant wanderings"}, {"id": "τηλέπλανος-note1", "translation": "Thus Seidler for τηλέπλαγκτοι [far-wandering]."}, {"id": "τηλέπλανος-quote1", "translation": "Where are the far-wandering wanderings leading me?"}, {"id": "τηλέπλανος-word1", "translation": "far-wandering"}, {"id": "τηλέπομπος-orth1", "translation": "sent from afar"}, {"id": "τηλέπομπος-def1", "translation": "sent from afar"}, {"id": "τηλέπομπος-quote1", "translation": "the watch did not refuse the light sent from afar"}, {"id": "τήλεφος-orth1", "translation": "Telephus"}, {"id": "τήλεφος-def1", "translation": "Telephus, son of Hercules. Telephus was the title of a play of Aeschylus (fr. 236 237)."}, {"id": "τήλεφος-word1", "translation": "Telephus"}, {"id": "τηλικοῦτος-orth1", "translation": "of such an age, so old"}, {"id": "τηλικοῦτος-def1", "translation": "advanced to that age"}, {"id": "τηλικοῦτος-quote1", "translation": "hard for one of such an age to learn"}, {"id": "τηλουρός-orth1", "translation": "whose boundaries are far off, distant"}, {"id": "τηλουρός-def1", "translation": "whose boundaries are far off, distant"}, {"id": "τηλουρός-quote1", "translation": "we have come to the far-off plain of the earth"}, {"id": "τηλουρός-quote2", "translation": "you will come to a far-off land"}, {"id": "τήνος-orth1", "translation": "Tenos"}, {"id": "τήνος-def1", "translation": "Tenos, one of the Cyclades islands"}, {"id": "τήνος-quote1", "translation": "Andros joining with Tenos"}, {"id": "τηξίθυμος-orth1", "translation": "melting the heart, consuming the spirit"}, {"id": "τηξίθυμος-def1", "translation": "melting the heart"}, {"id": "τηξίθυμος-note1", "translation": "where Enger had conjectured θελξίθυμον [charming the heart]. Meineke in Philologus vol. 19 p. 200 proposed τηξίθυμον [melting the heart], comparing τηξίποθοι ἔρωτες [longings that melt desire], which Crates said in Clement of Alexandria, Stromata 2 p. 492. Neither conjecture is necessary."}, {"id": "τηξίθυμος-quote1", "translation": "the heart-biting flower of love"}, {"id": "τηξίθυμος-word1", "translation": "charming the heart"}, {"id": "τηξίθυμος-word2", "translation": "melting the heart"}, {"id": "τηξίθυμος-word3", "translation": "longings that melt desire"}, {"id": "τηρεύς-orth1", "translation": "Tereus"}, {"id": "τηρεύς-def1", "translation": "Tereus, son of Mars, king of the Thracians, husband of Procne: hence the adjective Τήρειος and with diaeresis Τηρέϊος."}, {"id": "τηρεύς-quote1", "translation": "of the wife of Tereus"}, {"id": "τηρεύς-word1", "translation": "of Tereus"}, {"id": "τηρεύς-word2", "translation": "of Tereus (with diaeresis)"}, {"id": "τηρός-orth1", "translation": "guardian"}, {"id": "τηρός-def1", "translation": "guardian"}, {"id": "τηρός-note1", "translation": "A suspect word not known elsewhere, which the scholiast explained by φύλακα [guard]. Compare what is said under ῥάβδος [staff]."}, {"id": "τηρός-quote1", "translation": "or the guardian staff of the temple (ἡεροῦ M), or the leader of the city"}, {"id": "τηρός-word1", "translation": "guard"}, {"id": "τηρός-word2", "translation": "staff"}, {"id": "τιάρα-orth1", "translation": "tiara"}, {"id": "τιάρα-def1", "translation": "tiara, headdress among the Persians"}, {"id": "τιάρα-note1", "translation": "Thus from the copy for τιήρας."}, {"id": "τιάρα-quote1", "translation": "showing the cheek-piece of the royal tiara"}, {"id": "τιάρα-word1", "translation": "tiaras (acc. pl.)"}, {"id": "τιήρα-orth1", "translation": "See τιάρα."}, {"id": "τιήρα-def1", "translation": "See τιάρα."}, {"id": "τιήρα-word1", "translation": "tiara"}, {"id": "τιθασός-orth1", "translation": "tame, gentle"}, {"id": "τιθασός-def1", "translation": "tame, gentle"}, {"id": "τιθασός-note1", "translation": "Thus Turnebus for πίθασος φίλος [persuasive friend]."}, {"id": "τιθασός-quote1", "translation": "when Ares, being tame, takes a friend"}, {"id": "τιθασός-word1", "translation": "persuasive friend"}, {"id": "τίθημι-orth1", "translation": "to place, to put"}]}